  "id": "social-need",
  "term": "social need",
  "definition": "In this historical source, social need means the strong human requirement for companionship and nearness to other people, which is treated as basic to mental well-being. It also includes the need to keep the approval of one’s social group, shaping conduct toward conformity with its customs and regard for others.",
